content.text:
Run from `api`, replacing the email:

```bash
USER_EMAIL='your-user@email.com' npx prisma db execute --stdin <<'SQL'
DELETE FROM "Balance"
WHERE "userId" IN (SELECT "id" FROM "User" WHERE "email" = :'USER_EMAIL');

DELETE FROM "CartItem"
WHERE "userId" IN (SELECT "id" FROM "User" WHERE "email" = :'USER_EMAIL');

DELETE FROM "User"
WHERE "email" = :'USER_EMAIL';
SQL
```

Actually, Prisma `db execute` does **not** support `:'USER_EMAIL'` variables. Use the simple version with the real email pasted directly:

```bash
npx prisma db execute --stdin <<'SQL'
DELETE FROM "Balance" WHERE "userId" IN (SELECT "id" FROM "User" WHERE "email" = 'your-user@email.com');
DELETE FROM "CartItem" WHERE "userId" IN (SELECT "id" FROM "User" WHERE "email" = 'your-user@email.com');
DELETE FROM "User" WHERE "email" = 'your-user@email.com';
SQL
```

Then register the user again normally.

